+## Asset workarounds and evidence from failures
+
+Before rebuilding a font or another data asset, distinguish broken source data
+from rendering/runtime behavior. Check ready redistributable alternatives and
+explain the tradeoff (for example, changed font metrics versus preserving the
+existing layout). Do not imply that hand-editing outlines is the only remedy.
+
+For a font workaround:
+
+- Geometry validation is necessary but insufficient. Zero intersection flags
+  can coexist with filled counters, missing stems or merged disconnected parts.
+- Keep rejected candidates as negative fixtures. A new guard must fail on the
+  rejected asset and pass on the new one. Check counters, disconnected ink
+  components, advance widths and unrelated outlines, then actual small-size
+  rendering and the application at the user's DPI.
+- Normalize inconsistent source winding before offsetting. Resolve crossing
+  contours before choosing their direction, recheck after rounding, and preserve
+  gaps between disconnected components. Neither operation order nor topology
+  checks alone establish good font design.
+- Whole-face hinting can change rasterized metrics even with unchanged advances
+  in font units. State its scope and retain the user's visual feedback exactly.
+- Prefer temporary per-prefix selection with a finally rollback during research.
+  Record the actually selected face, not only that a resource was loaded.
+
+For a codec, test generic system discovery as well as direct COM activation,
+then exercise the actual app. Validate registration types and rollback on the
+native reference platform as well as Wine; Wine accepting a registry value is
+not evidence that its type is correct. Publish explicit format/color/metadata
+limits rather than silently claiming complete format support.
+
+After each attempt, state the current user-visible installation status:
+experimental build only, temporary test rolled back, permanently installed, or
+uninstalled. A successful temporary app test does not fix the user's ordinary
+app after rollback. Save failed hypotheses, harness/focus errors, timeouts,
+cache contamination and exact recovery beside successful results; never turn
+missing evidence into a passing check. Retain only sanitized public evidence.
+
